From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Cover the raw visible rect with the window surface in emulated display modes.

In an emulated display mode, map_window_rects_virt_to_raw keeps the window
and client rects' aspect ratio, but makes a fullscreen visible rect cover
the whole raw monitor. The window surface was still created by DPI
scaling the virtual visible rect, so the driver surface only covered the
scaled contents, while the driver places it at the raw visible rect's
origin.

GTA III sets 640x480 on a 3840x2160 monitor: the window is
(480,0)-(3360,2160), the raw visible rect the whole monitor, and the
driver surface was 2944x2304. On Wine-Wayland, the intro videos, which are
drawn into the window surface with GDI, were shown stretched from the left
edge of the screen, with the desktop visible on the right, until the
game's own D3D frames covered the window.

When the raw visible rect is larger than the scaled contents, create the
driver surface for the whole raw visible rect, draw the scaled contents at
their raw position in it, and paint the border around them black. The
scaled surface offsets its clip, shape and self-painted regions the same
way, and keeps the border in the clip region. Other windows are not
affected.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
+++ b/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
 /* dce.c */
 extern struct window_surface dummy_surface;
 extern void create_window_surface( HWND hwnd, BOOL create_layered, const RECT *surface_rect, UINT monitor_dpi,
+                                   const RECT *monitor_visible, const RECT *monitor_contents,
                                    struct window_surface **window_surface );
 extern struct window_surface *get_driver_window_surface( struct window_surface *surface, UINT monitor_dpi );
 extern void erase_now( HWND hwnd, UINT rdw_flags );
--- a/dlls/win32u/dce.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
@@ -672,6 +672,7 @@
